but I've become in the past decade or so comfortable enough with the study that I have to admit that I really never know for sure exactly why I did something. I mean sometimes I have a pretty good idea, but I certainly don't kid myself anymore to say that I even usually know why I do what I do. I mean there's just too much research, much of which you documented and reported on that shows that biases were completely unaware of, not just sometimes powerfully drive us in very particular direction.
